With this auth setup, an authenticated user sends a request to **update** a thread's metadata. What happens?

```python
@auth.on
async def reject_unhandled(ctx, value):
    raise Auth.exceptions.HTTPException(status_code=403, detail="Forbidden")

@auth.on.threads.create
async def on_thread_create(ctx, value):
    value.setdefault("metadata", {})["owner"] = ctx.user.identity
    return {"owner": ctx.user.identity}

@auth.on.threads.read
async def on_thread_read(ctx, value):
    return {"owner": ctx.user.identity}
```
